util/oslib-posix.c: tolerate ENOTTY in qemu_set_blocking()

Same Darwin behaviour: resetting O_NONBLOCK on a raw disk descriptor received
over SCM_RIGHTS fails with ENOTTY, the read is reported as an error and the
QMP connection is dropped, which kills add-fd for device descriptors.

Applies to QEMU 11.1.0 and 11.1.2 unchanged.

--- a/util/oslib-posix.c	2026-10-23 13:08:36
+++ b/util/oslib-posix.c	2026-10-23 13:08:36
@@ -255,6 +255,19 @@
     g_autoptr(GError) err = NULL;
 
     if (!g_unix_set_fd_nonblocking(fd, !block, &err)) {
+        /*
+         * Darwin rejects F_SETFL on a raw disk device node with ENOTTY for
+         * every value, including the flags the descriptor already carries, so
+         * there is nothing this could have changed. Treating it as fatal makes
+         * SCM_RIGHTS unusable for device descriptors: the O_NONBLOCK reset in
+         * qio_channel_socket_copy_fds() fails, the read is reported as an
+         * error, and the monitor connection is dropped -- which takes add-fd
+         * with it, and with it any way to hand a running QEMU a fresh
+         * descriptor for a device that has re-enumerated.
+         */
+        if (errno == ENOTTY) {
+            return true;
+        }
         error_setg_errno(errp, errno,
                          "Can't set file descriptor %d %s: %s", fd,
                          block ? "blocking" : "non-blocking",
